  "brief": "THE CASE IN FIVE LINES\n1. Clark Kerrigan, 39, lead collision estimator at Tri-County Collision & Frame, was found unresponsive in the estimator glass office on 2015-03-18; manner is homicide from two penetrating gunshot wounds to the torso (doc01, doc02).\n2. Medical Examiner set the wide window at 22:30–00:30 (doc02), while Clark Kerrigan's 23:46 outgoing SMS (doc10) narrows the working survival window to 23:46–00:30.\n3. Pauline Corbin gave a false Year-1 alibi (doc07) refuted by 22:56–23:18 ALPR crossings (doc09), but his 23:18 northbound exit and 23:36 cardlock swipe 16.2 miles away precede Clark Kerrigan's 23:46 SMS, corroborating his absence during the narrowed window.\n4. Derrick Berglund's departure account shows medium 6-year drift (doc12 vs. doc13), and the press rumor regarding the defective latch is neutralized by 2014 public inspection docket doc16.\n5. Local keypad memory failed at 23:12 (doc05) and utility interval microfilm (doc11) remains unpulled, leaving narrowed-window access uncorroborated alongside a 2-vs-1 CSI discrepancy, uncollected 23:39 photo, and untested DNA Item 3.\n\nSTRONGEST CONTRADICTION\nNo suspect's alibi inside the narrowed 23:46–00:30 window is contradicted yet because local keypad memory failed at 23:12 (doc05). The strongest pre-window conflict is Pauline Corbin's Year-1 denial vs. ALPR telemetry (resolved in doc08 and cleared of the post-23:46 window by doc09/doc10):\n- doc07: \"I was in Wexford County playing cards with friends from 20:30 until 01:15 and never drove anywhere near Tri-County Collision & Frame on 2015-03-17.\"\n- doc09: \"2015-03-17 22:56 — County Line Rd Gantry Southbound (toward Tri-County Collision & Frame), plate PDY-7035 (charcoal 2015 Nissan Altima, reg. Pauline Corbin).\"\n\nALIBI TABLE (Narrowed survival window 23:46–00:30 (within ME window 22:30–00:30))\n- Patricia Kowalski: UNCORROBORATED\n- Pauline Corbin: CORROBORATED (cleared of narrowed window by doc09 + doc10)\n- Derrick Berglund: UNCORROBORATED (MEDIUM multi-year drift, doc12 vs. doc13)\n- Hector Wilkins: UNCORROBORATED (22:48 entry confirmed by doc05; no exit log)\n\nTOP THREE LEADS\n1. (60 pts, 25 + 20 + 15 = 60) Subpoena and pull the off-site alarm vendor's serial audit backup reel referenced in doc05 covering 23:12 through 00:30 to recover post-battery-fault PIN unlocks.\n2. (60 pts, 25 + 20 + 15 = 60) Submit preserved biological trace swab Item 3 from Property Clerk ledger doc15 to the state forensic laboratory for modern STR and touch-DNA profiling.\n3. (60 pts, 25 + 20 + 15 = 60) Pull unindexed utility microfilm Box referenced in doc11 to obtain 15-minute sub-circuit load strip charts across 22:30–00:30.\n\nGAP LIST\n- Post-23:12 door-access serial backup reel and 15-minute utility sub-meter microfilm were never pulled.\n- Marker 5 count discrepancy: two spent 9mm Luger brass shell casings observed in scene report but only one booked in Property Clerk ledger.\n- Original digital file and EXIF metadata for the 23:39 patron photograph were never collected or booked.\n- Exterior municipal/commercial camera facing the property was never pulled.\n- Preserved biological swab Item 3 remains sealed and untested for STR/touch DNA.\n\nThis board judges the file. The detective does the detecting."
