  "brief": "THE CASE IN FIVE LINES\n1. Monique Yates, 48, overnight commissary manager at Redline 24hr Truck Plaza, was found unresponsive in the back commissary safe office on 2017-03-10; manner is homicide from two penetrating .380 gunshot wounds to the chest (doc01, doc02).\n2. Medical Examiner set the wide window at 22:36–00:36 (doc02), while Monique Yates's 23:52 outgoing SMS (doc10) and 23:59 PIN 3632 unlock (doc05) narrow the survival floor to 23:59–00:36.\n3. Wesley Lomax gave a false Year-1 alibi (doc07) refuted by 23:02–23:24 ALPR crossings (doc09), but his 23:24 northbound exit and 23:42 cardlock swipe 16.2 miles away precede Monique Yates's 23:52 SMS, corroborating his absence during the narrowed window.\n4. Sterling Ibarra's departure account shows medium 6-year drift (doc12 vs. doc13), and the press rumor regarding the defective latch is neutralized by 2016 public inspection docket doc16.\n5. Master PIN 9054 (assigned to Garrett Stanton) unlocked the back commissary safe office at 00:13 (doc05) and circuit load ran until 00:25 (doc11), while CSI notes a 2-vs-1 marker 5 discrepancy, an uncollected 23:45 photo, and an unpulled exterior camera.\n\nSTRONGEST CONTRADICTION\nGarrett Stanton's denial of unlocking or entering the back commissary safe office conflicts with the keypad export:\n- doc03: \"I never entered the back commissary safe office at any point that night. On my rounds I only check the exterior handle from the corridor.\"\n- doc05: \"2017-03-10 00:13 — PIN 9054 UNLOCK\" (paired with doc05 PIN schedule assigning 9054 to Garrett Stanton, and doc11 load drop at 00:25).\n\nALIBI TABLE (Narrowed survival window 23:59–00:36 (within ME window 22:36–00:36))\n- Garrett Stanton: CONTRADICTED\n- Wesley Lomax: CORROBORATED (cleared of narrowed window by doc09 + doc10)\n- Sterling Ibarra: UNCORROBORATED (MEDIUM multi-year drift, doc12 vs. doc13)\n- Grant Quinn: UNCORROBORATED (22:54 entry confirmed by doc05; no exit log)\n\nTOP THREE LEADS\n1. (80 pts, 40 + 25 + 15 = 80) Have the detective re-interview Garrett Stanton in person and ask why master PIN 9054 unlocked the back commissary safe office strike at 00:13 (doc05) while doc03 denies entering and doc04 logs only a corridor handle check.\n2. (80 pts, 40 + 25 + 15 = 80) Have the detective re-interview Garrett Stanton in person regarding the high-severity contradiction between his 23:00 dark-office claim (doc03) and the AMI sub-meter load continuing until 00:25 (doc11).\n3. (60 pts, 25 + 20 + 15 = 60) Submit preserved biological trace swab Item 3 from Property Clerk ledger doc15 to the state forensic laboratory for STR and touch-DNA testing.\n\nGAP LIST\n- Marker 5 count discrepancy: two spent .380 ACP brass shell casings observed in scene report but only one booked in Property Clerk ledger.\n- Original digital file and EXIF metadata for the 23:45 patron photograph were never collected or booked.\n- Exterior municipal/commercial camera facing the property was never pulled.\n- Preserved biological swab Item 3 remains sealed and untested for STR/touch DNA.\n\nThis board judges the file. The detective does the detecting."
