  "brief": "THE CASE IN FIVE LINES\n1. Curtis Lindqvist, 53, evening lanes manager at Starlight 24-Lane Lounge, was found unresponsive in the cashier counting office on 2018-04-15; manner is homicide from blunt force trauma to the head (doc01, doc02).\n2. Medical Examiner set the wide window at 22:30–00:30 (doc02), while Curtis Lindqvist's 23:46 outgoing SMS (doc10) and 23:53 PIN 2755 unlock (doc05) narrow the survival floor to 23:53–00:30.\n3. Sylvia Vogel gave a false Year-1 alibi (doc07) refuted by 22:56–23:18 ALPR crossings (doc09), but his 23:18 northbound exit and 23:36 cardlock swipe 16.2 miles away precede Curtis Lindqvist's 23:46 SMS, corroborating his absence during the narrowed window.\n4. Darnell Haddad's departure account shows medium 6-year drift (doc12 vs. doc13), and the press rumor regarding the defective latch is neutralized by 2017 public inspection docket doc16.\n5. Master PIN 9038 (assigned to Vera Tran) unlocked the cashier counting office at 00:07 (doc05) and circuit load ran until 00:19 (doc11), while CSI notes a 2-vs-1 marker 5 discrepancy, an uncollected 23:39 photo, and an unpulled exterior camera.\n\nSTRONGEST CONTRADICTION\nVera Tran's denial of unlocking or entering the cashier counting office conflicts with the keypad export:\n- doc03: \"I never entered the cashier counting office at any point that night. On my rounds I only check the exterior handle from the corridor.\"\n- doc05: \"2018-04-15 00:07 — PIN 9038 UNLOCK\" (paired with doc05 PIN schedule assigning 9038 to Vera Tran, and doc11 load drop at 00:19).\n\nALIBI TABLE (Narrowed survival window 23:53–00:30 (within ME window 22:30–00:30))\n- Vera Tran: CONTRADICTED\n- Sylvia Vogel: CORROBORATED (cleared of narrowed window by doc09 + doc10)\n- Darnell Haddad: UNCORROBORATED (MEDIUM multi-year drift, doc12 vs. doc13)\n- Devin Lockwood: UNCORROBORATED (22:48 entry confirmed by doc05; no exit log)\n\nTOP THREE LEADS\n1. (80 pts, 40 + 25 + 15 = 80) Have the detective re-interview Vera Tran in person and ask why master PIN 9038 unlocked the cashier counting office strike at 00:07 (doc05) while doc03 denies entering and doc04 logs only a corridor handle check.\n2. (80 pts, 40 + 25 + 15 = 80) Have the detective re-interview Vera Tran in person regarding the high-severity contradiction between his 23:00 dark-office claim (doc03) and the AMI sub-meter load continuing until 00:19 (doc11).\n3. (60 pts, 25 + 20 + 15 = 60) Submit preserved biological trace swab Item 3 from Property Clerk ledger doc15 to the state forensic laboratory for STR and touch-DNA testing.\n\nGAP LIST\n- Marker 5 count discrepancy: two torn tamper-evident bank deposit bag stubs observed in scene report but only one booked in Property Clerk ledger.\n- Original digital file and EXIF metadata for the 23:39 patron photograph were never collected or booked.\n- Exterior municipal/commercial camera facing the property was never pulled.\n- Preserved biological swab Item 3 remains sealed and untested for STR/touch DNA.\n\nThis board judges the file. The detective does the detecting."
